<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leo III the Isaurian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 717–741 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Emperor Leo III</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leo III the Isaurian was a Byzantine emperor who reigned from 717 to 741 and founded the Isaurian dynasty. He successfully defended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> against the great Arab siege of 717 to 718, a decisive moment in the survival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>. He is also associated with the beginning of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-iconoclasm">Iconoclast controversy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leo-iii-the-isaurian.jpg" alt="Leo III the Isaurian" width="320" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solidus_of_Leo_III_sb1504.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
